== 1. a parent re-render with no parameter change ==
ok   everything rendered once: 1/1/1
ok   the parent rendered again: 2
ok   the memoized child did NOT: 1
ok   THE CONTROL: the plain child did: 2

== 2. a parameter that actually changed ==
ok   the memoized child rendered: 2
ok   and the html is the new value: <ul><li>a/2/false</li><li>a</li></ul>

== 3. every scalar kind moves it, one at a time ==
ok   a string parameter: 3
ok   a bool parameter: 4
ok   and changing it back is a change too: 5

== 4. a fresh Callback every render is not a change ==
ok   the memoized child still declined: 5
ok   THE CONTROL: the plain one still rendered: 7

== 5. what the startup scan refuses ==
ok   three, and no more: 3
ok   a @memo that is not a component: latte$entry.NotAComponent is annotated @memo but does not extend latte.Component, so nothing would ever consult it
ok   a parameter it cannot compare: latte$entry.TakesAList.rows is a @param of type List<string> on a @memo component, and latte cannot compare one — only string, int, bool and float. Write should_render yourself, or drop @memo
ok   a component that takes child content: latte$entry.TakesContent.body is a @param of type fn(latte.Builder) -> unit on a @memo component — a closure the parent rebuilds every render, holding markup that may be completely different. Its parameters can all be equal while its content is not. Drop @memo, or take the content another way
ok   THE CONTROL: a @memo that works is not named: false

== 6. ParamWatch by hand still works ==
ok   a fresh watch has recorded nothing: true
ok   the first record is always a change: true
ok   the same values are not: false
ok   a different one is: true
